  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Just behind Toulon station, the Parc des Lices is a city-centre green space redeveloped by the City and the Métropole, presented in March 2026: meadows, planted beds, paths for pedestrians, bikes and rollerbladers, a playground, a zip line, a multisport court, a street workout station and a dog park dedicated to dogs. A micro-forest of 390 Mediterranean trees has been planted to bring coolness, and LED lighting lets you enjoy the park in the evening. In its list of dog-dedicated places, the City specifies that the park's dog area has an agility zone.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The park is not off-limits to dogs: the City of Toulon reminds visitors that a leash is compulsory throughout the municipality, with dog areas where dogs can move freely, including the one at Les Lices. The Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur Tourisme page likewise says "animals accepted on a leash only", with a dog park, free entry, public toilets and a picnic area.</p>
      <p>Picking up waste is compulsory throughout the municipality, including inside the dog parks: more than 300 bag dispensers are spread around the city, and waste not picked up can mean a €135 fine. For a question about dog areas, the town hall's urban animal service can be reached on 04 94 36 30 26.</p>
      <p>The City's page publishes no opening times. The Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur Tourisme page announces 9am-7pm every day from 1 September 2026 to 30 June 2027 (9am-9pm from 1 July to 31 August 2026); the summer 2027 hours are not yet published. To confirm, call 04 94 36 83 30 (number on the page) or the town hall (04 94 36 30 00). The Métropole announces nearly 9,200 m² for the redeveloped park.</p>
      <p>The City also has some thirty "canisites", including 15 fenced dog parks of more than 100 m², a dog course at Les Lices and a dog swimming area with a launch ramp at the Anse Tabarly (Mourillon beach): in these areas, dogs can run or swim off the leash. The Faron massif also welcomes dogs, which travel free on the cable car. Conversely, some of the city's green spaces are off-limits to dogs, even on a leash: the City's list marks them with a pictogram.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the dog park lets you safely let your dog off the leash; elsewhere in the park, a leash is required.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Toulon station and the city centre are a short walk away, handy for combining the stroll with other stops during the day.</p>
